    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Gordon Hughes Estate Agents are delighted to present 60 Jamestown Park to the market, an attractive four bedroomed semi-detached home ideally positioned in the ever-popular Jamestown Park development in Ratoath. \n\nExtending to approx. 123sqm, this well-proportioned home offers generous accommodation and excellent potential for modern family living. The property benefits from an attractive Tudor-style façade, with the front elevation complemented by mature planting and a spacious cobble lock driveway providing ample off-street parking. \n\nOn entering, the property offers a welcoming sense of space, with well-balanced accommodation throughout and excellent potential for the new owners to put their own stamp on the home. The layout is ideally suited to family life, with four bedrooms and three bathrooms providing comfortable accommodation for growing families, first time buyers or these looking to trade up. To the rear the property enjoys a private and mature rear garden, which is predominantly laid in lawn.\n\nJamestown Park is a highly regarded residential development, with Ratoath offering an excellent choice of schools, shops, sporting facilities, restaurants and everyday amenities. The development is well positioned for commuters, making this an attractive location for those seeking a balance between 'village' living and accessibility to Dublin. \n\nViewing is highly recommended!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall 2.36m x 5.92m \nA generous welcome to this home fitted with wide plank, walnut effect laminate flooring, coving, ceiling roses and useful understairs storage. Also hosts Guest WC 1.55m x 1.75m which is fitted with wc and whb, tiled flooring and sink splashback. \n\nLivingroom 3.85m x 5.87m \nA fantastic sized living room with bay window - fitted with semi-solid wooden flooring, coving, ceiling rose, wall lights and central fireplace with gas insert. Double doors lead through to…. \n\nDining room 3.19m x 4.16m \nFitted with wide plank laminate flooring, coving, ceiling rose and sliding patio doors out to the rear garden. Arch leads through to…\n\nKitchen/Breakfast Room 2.68m x 6.16m\nFitted with modern shaker wall and floor units, wide plank laminate flooring and subway tiled splashback. Arch through to Utility nook 1.55m x 0.84m which is plumbed for washing machine.\n\nLanding 2.19m x 3.89m \nSpacious landing which hosts hot-press and provides access to the attic. \n\nMaster Bedroom 3.24m x 4.07m \nA generous master bedroom which is located to the front of the property and fitted with built in wardrobes. \n\nEn-Suite 2.44m x 1.45m \nFully tiled and fitted with wc, whb and shower. \n\nBedroom 2 3.02m x 3.61m \nLocated to the rear of the property fitted with T&G flooring and built in wardrobes. \n\nBedroom 3 2.87m x 2.45m \nAlso located to the rear of the property.\n\nBedroom 4 2.54m x 2.79m \nLocated to the front of the property fitted with built in wardrobes. \n\nBathroom 1.78m x 1.99m \nCentral main bathroom which is fully tiled and fitted with wc, whb and bath with shower attachment."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Attractive four bedroomed semi-detached home.\nWell-proportioned accommodation of c. 130sqm.\nIdeally position in this sought after development.\nNot overlooked to the front & private, mature rear garden. \nServices: Gas fired central heating, mains water and mains sewage. \nBER: C2. BER Number: 106996382\nBuilt c. 2000\nConvenient location close to Ratoath Village and local amenities."
      },
